## Creating a function to calculate the mean of a numeric vector, then compare to R's built-in mean() function.

### Create a function

```{r, eval=TRUE, echo=TRUE, message=FALSE, warning=FALSE, class.source = "fold-show", fig.height=5, fig.width=8, results='show', cache=FALSE}

#### Create a function to calculate the mean of numeric vector####
calc_mean <- function(x) {
  if(!is.numeric(x)){
    stop("Input must be a numeric vector.")
  }
  
  #### take the sum of all the numeric vector####
  sum <- 0
  for (i in 1:length(x)) {
    sum <- sum +x[i]
  }
  
  ####calculate the mean ####
  mean <- sum / length(x)
  
  return(mean)
}
```

