```

### The code is a for loop that iterates over values *i* from 1-4 sequentially. Inside the loop, the code takes the i-th row of matrix *m*, and assigns is to the temporary variable *temp*. However, the matrix only consists of 3 rows and will execute the loop for i=1-3 until it 1=4 which will try to access a non-existent row. The result is an error message printed, *Error in m[i, ] : subscript out of bounds*. This causes the program to exit the loop without executing the last line of code, which was intended to append the values in *temp* to the *numbers* vector at each iteration of the loop.

```{r, eval=FALSE, echo=TRUE, message=FALSE, warning=FALSE, class.source = "fold-show", fig.height=5, fig.width=8, results='show', cache=FALSE}
